              ToolMessage(content="I've found excellent options. Given that today is September 2026, I searched for **2027** dates — and picked the two best wedding seasons in Paris: late spring (May–June) and early autumn (September), when the weather is gorgeous and the city is at its most romantic.\n\nHere's my shortlist of the best one-way flights from London to Paris:\n\n### 💰 Cheapest Options\n| Route | Times | Duration | Cabin | Price |\n|-------|-------|----------|-------|-------|\n| SEN → CDG (easyJet) | 13 May 10:10 → 12:20 | 1h 10m | Economy | **55 EUR** |\n| SEN → CDG (easyJet) | 07 Jun 11:10 → 13:20 | 1h 10m | Economy | **58 EUR** |\n| LGW → CDG (easyJet) | 16 May 08:10 → 10:30 | 1h 20m | Economy | 61 EUR |\n| LTN → CDG (easyJet) | 07 Sep 19:10 → 21:30 | 1h 20m | Economy | 64 EUR |\n\n### ⚡ Shortest Options (~1h 10m non-stop)\n| Route | Times | Duration | Cabin | Price |\n|-------|-------|----------|-------|-------|\n| SEN → CDG (easyJet) | 13 May 10:10 → 12:20 | **1h 10m** | Economy | 55 EUR |\n| SEN → CDG (easyJet) | 14 May 11:20 → 13:30 | 1h 10m | Economy | 64 EUR |\n| SEN → CDG (easyJet) | 16 May 07:25 → 09:35 | 1h 10m | Economy | 70 EUR |\n\n### ✨ Other Notable Options\n| Route | Times | Duration | Cabin | Price |\n|-------|-------|----------|-------|-------|\n| SEN → CDG (easyJet) | 10 Jun 10:10 → 12:20 | 1h 10m | Economy | 65 EUR |\n| LGW → CDG (easyJet) | 08 Sep 08:00 → 10:20 | 1h 20m | Economy | 69 EUR |\n| LHR → CDG (Air France) | 08 Sep 15:20 → 17:40 | 1h 20m | Economy | 122 EUR |\n| STN → BGY → BVA (Ryanair) | 08 Sep 15:25 → 21:30 | 5h 05m | Economy | 100 EUR |\n\n---\n\n## 🏆 My Recommendation\n\n**The winner:** **London Southend (SEN) → Paris CDG on 13 May 2027, easyJet U25711 — €55, non-stop in 1h 10m.** It's simultaneously the cheapest *and* the shortest option, ticking both your top criteria. May is ideal for a Paris wedding: mild temperatures, long sunny days, and the gardens (perfect for photos) are in full bloom.\n\n**Runner-up:** If you prefer departing from a more central airport, the **Gatwick → CDG easyJet flights at €61–€69** are nearly as cheap with the same quick ~1h 20m hop — and for a full-service experience, **Air France from Heathrow (€122)** is the premium choice, landing you right at CDG with more flexible baggage options.\n\nAll flights land at **Charles de Gaulle**, well connected to central Paris. For the shortest journeys aim for the May/June dates — early autumn (September) is also lovely, just slightly pricier.\n\n---\n\n🛫 *Bon voyage! Fun fact: Paris's Charles de Gaulle Airport's terminal 2 was designed by the same architect as the Louvre's famous glass pyramid — getting married and simply arriving in Paris both get you a masterpiece.* 🗼", name='search_flights', id='ee88b2b3-0e04-4e11-bad8-8b561732d69c', tool_call_id='call_6808fbccc8694784b326223b'),
              ToolMessage(content="I've completed my searches (12 searches). Here's my summary of the best wedding venue options in Paris for 100 guests, balancing the three criteria: **lowest price**, **exact capacity of 100**, and **highest reviews**.\n\n## Top Recommendations (Paris, 100 guests)\n\n### 🏆 Best Overall Value + Reviews\n**1. UICP Espaces** — Paris\n- **Price:** €1,500 – €10,000 (venue hire)\n- **Capacity:** 10–300 (flexible rooms easily sized for 100)\n- **Reviews:** ⭐ 5.0 (43 reviews) — highest-rated option\n- Flexible spaces that adapt to ceremony → cocktail → seated dinner → dance party.\n\n**2. La Fabrique République** — 10th arrondissement\n- **Price:** €3,500 – €8,000\n- **Capacity:** Up to 150 seated / 250 standing (comfortable for 100)\n- **Reviews:** ⭐ 5.0 (37 reviews)\n- Industrial-chic 700 m² loft near Place de la République; praised for beautiful décor and attentive staff.\n\n### 💰 Lowest Price Options (Exact 100 Capacity)\n**3. Le Camondo** — Paris\n- **Price:** €1,000 – €8,400 (very lowest starting point)\n- **Capacity:** 100 guests\n- **Reviews:** No reviews yet (new listing) — a slight risk, but the cheapest match. Restaurant with garden/veranda spaces; external catering permitted.\n\n**4. La Maison de Charly** — Paris\n- **Price:** €4,000 – €6,000\n- **Capacity:** 100 dining / 150 reception (exact match)\n- **Reviews:** 6 reviews (Bridebook)\n- Fully privatizable restaurant/bar with dance floor and sound system; church within walking distance.\n\n### ⭐ Highly Rated Alternatives (Can Host 100)\n**5. Péniche Le Grand Bleu** — Seine river barge, Paris\n- **Price:** From ~€900 (very low entry)\n- **Capacity:** Up to 120 guests\n- **Reviews:** ⭐ 5.0 (27 reviews) — glowing reviews for food and staff. Memorable floating venue experience.\n\n**6. L'Usine Deguerry** — near Place de la République\n- **Price:** €6,120 – €9,060\n- **Capacity:** 100 guests (exact)\n- **Reviews:** ⭐ 5.0 (4 reviews, limited sample)\n\n**7. Bleu Seine** — Seine river barge fleet\n- **Price:** €3,000 – €7,500; packages from €119/person\n- **Capacity:** Multiple boats that fit 100 (e.g., Dauphin 30–120, Ivory 30–96)\n- Iconic Eiffel Tower backdrop; customizable.\n\n### Luxury tier (for comparison, if budget allows)\n- **Le George** (Pompidou rooftop): up to 100 guests, from €15,000\n- **Four Seasons George V / Peninsula Paris**: palace hotels with 100-guest ballrooms, €18,750+/person packages (very premium)\n\n## Key Notes\n- **Best balance of all three criteria:** UICP Espaces and La Fabrique République — both 5.0-rated, reasonably priced, and proven for ~100-guest weddings.\n- **Cheapest exact-100 match:** Le Camondo (from €1,000) and La Maison de Charly (€4,000–6,000).\n- **Watch out for:** Many Paris venues quote venue hire only; catering and minimum spends are often additional (Palace hotels can push totals to €40k–150k for 100 guests). Always confirm inclusive catering and any minimum night/guest requirements.", name='search_venues', id='7d3f8ff0-0b95-4946-946f-056e8a0887d4', tool_call_id='call_1eeb71a392a0402690dce518'),
